.TH "KC" "1" "Jan 0001" "kc dev" "kc Manual"

.SH NAME
kc-rollback - Restore a previously recorded value of a secret


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBkc rollback KEY [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Restores a recorded version as the live value. The value being replaced is
itself recorded first, so a rollback is never destructive and can be undone.
Without --version the most recent recorded value is restored.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for rollback

.PP
\fB--version\fP=0
	version to restore (default: the most recent)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--vault\fP=""
	target vault (overrides active vault)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBkc(1)\fP
